#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091902 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "a7f1c431-54b4-52b5-9ad6-cb4dd81e0f30" :question/math-academy-id "e-151" :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-1.0$ | $-0.7$ | $-0.3$ | $0.7$ | $1.5$ | $2.1$ |\n\nApproximate  at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+1)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4)-f(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-0.3)-(-0.7)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.4}{1} \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091903 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/id #uuid "8717eda6-57e6-59ec-ab1c-f40887fa52fb" :question/math-academy-id "e-152" :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown below. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/3084d6ae67f37517f3d8ad0a9a62be05fe1906fcc2a24f69bd29a1e00dfd0373.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\frac{g(x+h) - g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4.$  Applying the above formula with $x=4$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+2)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(6)-g(4)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091904 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "580533af-c13d-5e1c-8282-f0172709c7e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-153" :question/problem "The position of a race car along a straight track, measured in feet from the starting line, is given by the function $s(t),$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. The values of $s(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $3$ | $7$ | $12$ | $19$ |\n\nApproximate the velocity $s'(t)$ at the time $t=0.1$ using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\ns'(t) \\approx \\frac{s(t+h) - s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=0.1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(0.1) & ≈\\frac{s(0.1+0.1)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(0.2)-s(0.1)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-3}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.1} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=0.1$ the velocity is approximately $40\\, \\textrm{ft}/\\textrm{s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091905 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "73818e0b-6f95-59a6-b1a7-672bbea8de86" :question/math-academy-id "e-154" :question/problem "An oil tank has leaked $q(t)$ liters of oil after $t$ hours. The graph of $q(t)$ is shown below. Approximate the rate at which the oil is leaking from the tank when $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/b6c5286dae7e739a588173bad9c721ae34d07f86e455e44ec9f229628cf54211.png)" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\nq'(t) \\approx \\frac{q(t+h) - q(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=1$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{q(1+1)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{q(2)-q(1)}{1} \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $1$ hour, the tank is leaking oil at a rate of approximately $1\\,\\textrm{liter}/ \\textrm{hour}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9caecc5d-8440-591f-94ab-128cafe9ec7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336479} {:answer/id #uuid "e59dc82f-546e-5054-bfaf-c42e76ef5fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9caecc5d-8440-591f-94ab-128cafe9ec7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336479} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a1f5b66-8134-5091-8a35-8e0a994c04cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d82fcd9-f4c5-508c-af92-d0f336d3879f" :question/math-academy-id "q-313343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/204afb23fc438b047c72d6233b59b70c4741ee16a30a57c084682a3d14fd2188.png)\n\nA thin soap film is stretching over time. The graph of its surface area $A(t)$, in square centimeters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the surface area at $t=2$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nAfter $2$ minutes, the surface area increases at a rate of {{field-1}} ${\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{A(t+h)-A(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=2$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{A(2+2)-A(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{A(4)-A(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-10}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $2$ minutes, the surface area changes at a rate of approximately $15\\text{ }{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de5c37d3-ec60-55e8-99d0-3c3c22a5d090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336483} {:answer/id #uuid "fbdbd2f5-dc18-51c7-bf03-c9416c70d648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbdbd2f5-dc18-51c7-bf03-c9416c70d648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336484} :answer-field/id #uuid "16a8f30e-e511-558a-8e0a-3dc280f5acd3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f572f1e1-b5c8-5dc8-920b-f57ce4ebd415" :question/math-academy-id "q-341994" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.4$ | $1.1$ | $3.7$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.6) & ≈\\frac{g(0.6+0.3)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0.9)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.1-(-0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.3} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336485 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c3ef3de-b9a8-5700-a3c5-bc3c04dd32a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c3ef3de-b9a8-5700-a3c5-bc3c04dd32a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336487} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9100525-5208-51f6-afb2-5e3a7429aa6c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1e3efff-e4fc-5ebb-adad-78ad4184693c" :question/math-academy-id "q-341996" :question/problem "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $20.4$ | $18.6$ | $16.5$ | $14.4$ | $12.3$ | $10.8$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{g(2+2)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.4-16.5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.1}{2} \\\\  & =-1.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44f09c22-7107-5c80-9c91-a7b58cb639b2" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b8265b8-d983-5ed0-bc43-002b30c154f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b8265b8-d983-5ed0-bc43-002b30c154f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336490} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0ee1a1-21fb-578f-afca-2b23263b2356" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336489}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b775af5-e0be-50b8-a8d6-c6f7547ce3b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342003" :question/problem "A function $d(y)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $d(y)$ | $-8.92$ | $-11.34$ | $-15.23$ | $-17.56$ | $-18.21$ | $-18.50$ |\n\nApproximate ${d}^{′}(y)$ at the point $y=-5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${d}^{′}(-5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{d}^{′}(y)≈\\frac{d(y+h)-d(y)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $y=-5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(-5) & ≈\\frac{d(-5+2)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{d(-3)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11.34-(-8.92)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.42}{2} \\\\  & =-1.21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6456cccc-0cc9-5ecf-92ce-2dbbeede2972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6456cccc-0cc9-5ecf-92ce-2dbbeede2972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336493} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e61e8ba-c70b-5c12-8e33-d8d353588f6e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ed1d3b2-7869-51db-81ee-b2ccc32ccf11" :question/math-academy-id "q-342037" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/c51e6206f77b63181f6c9f67b116ba5c0024886c061e8c15fe10edab87c87e03.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3.$ Applying the above formula with $x=3$ and $h=2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+2)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3-5}{2} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f2ba0ab-900f-5b23-afe3-8e9ebaca0f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336496} {:answer/id #uuid "ba95476f-1be3-51f2-b940-a27e388ae9d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f2ba0ab-900f-5b23-afe3-8e9ebaca0f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336496} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7a6b482-53c5-577a-8e9e-c09454d3673f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70e8b70f-3021-53a3-b823-74d92203bf17" :question/math-academy-id "q-342038" :question/problem "The volume of water in a tank was recorded over time for $25$ minutes, starting from time $t=0$ minutes. The following table shows the volume $V(t)$, in liters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V(t)$ | $120$ | $150$ | $165$ | $180$ | $215$ | $240$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of volume at time $t=5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=5,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} liters per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{V(t+h)-V(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{V(5+5)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{V(10)-V(5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{165-150}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=5$ the rate of change was approximately $3$ liters per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b923956b-e419-5ddd-b919-0bd30634ed97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b923956b-e419-5ddd-b919-0bd30634ed97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336500} :answer-field/id #uuid "45c82cc2-134c-5f6d-b9d2-ea921d99cf28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c44cb097-7152-5126-bd0e-9033f85fd6ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-342040" :question/problem "A hiker’s elevation was recorded over time for $6$ hours, starting from time $t=0$ hours. The following table shows the elevation $E(t)$, in meters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $E(t)$ | $0$ | $200$ | $310$ | $395$ | $450$ | $525$ | $600$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of elevation at time $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=1,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} meters per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{E}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{E(t+h)-E(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{E(1+1)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{E(2)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{310-200}{1} \\\\  & =110.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=1$ the rate of change was approximately $110$ meters per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca988ad1-34e6-5afc-a468-61832cf2a285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca988ad1-34e6-5afc-a468-61832cf2a285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336503} :answer-field/id #uuid "257cf450-86c1-5a9d-987c-e360972cb657" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "408ca6b1-3ddb-58f1-8b96-44e416ee959f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342075" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/d84ba0a07821011be4cf5958af44ea73e97493c5a796a0324b068fe2adca8a12.png)\n\nA car is using petrol as it travels. The graph of the amount of petrol $P(d)$, in liters, remaining in the fuel tank after traveling a distance of $d$ miles is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the amount of petrol at $d=150$ using a forward difference with step size $h=50.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the amount of petrol decreases.\n\nAfter traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is {{field-1}} liters per mile." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(d)≈\\frac{P(d+h)-P(d)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the distance $d=150$ with step size $h=50.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(150) & ≈\\frac{P(150+50)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(200)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-30}{50} \\\\  & =-0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is $-0.4$ liters per mile."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29d6424-c745-5f0f-9f1d-a47b5c80cbc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29d6424-c745-5f0f-9f1d-a47b5c80cbc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336506} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a20db44-2111-5ec2-9b1b-28d00d485b8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfa3059e-2dcb-5fa2-abb3-d25cbe930e7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342079" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/846fc347c71ada4c01a5a85aabd0722203b84edbafcbe462064ae31d1cf2adbb.png)\n\nA drone is descending toward the ground. The graph of its height $H(t)$, in meters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the height at $t=9$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the height decreases.\n\nAfter $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is {{field-1}} meters per minute." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{H}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{H(t+h)-H(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=9$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{′}(9) & ≈\\frac{H(9+2)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(11)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-80}{2} \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is $-40$ meters per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa218d2d-e025-53fe-ab29-dc986fde4c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa218d2d-e025-53fe-ab29-dc986fde4c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336509} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbeb63ae-4e3e-5c1a-9159-eb9d96349c78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2642c08d-d846-51fe-9494-87c5a3d1bf87" :question/math-academy-id "q-342080" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/ae57faa04abd053e4a58d751cc084d58e07e84e0520c99a33a122f58dfd8f18c.png)\n\nA slice of jackfruit is placed in an air dryer. The graph of the moisture content $M(t)$, in percent, after $t$ hours is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the moisture content at $t=3$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the content decreases.\n\nAfter $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is {{field-1}} percent per hour." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{M(3+2)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(5)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-40}{2} \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is $-10$ percent per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b45839c3-7499-59ab-8faa-e0d148ee2a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336512} {:answer/id #uuid "0b0ebc80-d294-5f1b-bd94-0dd7b0bf031e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336513} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a88dd3-6060-544d-ba70-4ef6c2975bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336514} {:answer/id #uuid "0832afa2-2713-598b-924f-00733470ebe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336515} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e75a82-4cbb-54e8-876d-0ef10e4cdf74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0832afa2-2713-598b-924f-00733470ebe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336515} :answer-field/id #uuid "997ef771-7667-56c3-b41b-61101242d3e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336511}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5d32ddd-0763-54da-be13-1a93cdb99dff" :question/math-academy-id "q-47378" :question/problem "Andrey wants to estimate his running speed. Andrey's friend Max takes note of Andrey's position while he is on the track. Max's observations are given in the table below, where $s(t)$ is the distance covered, measured in meters, $t$ seconds after Andrey started running.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $4$ | $9$ | $15$ | $20$ | $27$ |\n\nApproximate Andrey's speed at the point where $t=6$ seconds using a forward difference approximation." :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{s(t+h)-s(t)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{s(6+2)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{s(8)-s(6)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $t=6$ Andrey's speed is approximately $2.5\\,\\text{m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e651cb4-ae24-5ac7-9c01-d90de562b155" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Table Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9afe2e83-8fa2-509a-a4f0-c4e386f18fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.8liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090450} {:answer/id #uuid "d0021242-94fd-580a-9fa4-a2d263311fb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090451} {:answer/id #uuid "154c9ed4-50dd-5af2-95dd-1e06ee41f8b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.6liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090452} {:answer/id #uuid "72e2b97f-23b4-51ae-bc4c-08babf085e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.6liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090453} {:answer/id #uuid "76e3a6c9-c700-5972-a662-5ac8be338a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.2liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9afe2e83-8fa2-509a-a4f0-c4e386f18fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.8liters/mile" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090450} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7a34b84-9257-5e81-8109-61045e5b92d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95a18afa-f8fa-5bdd-82d9-85c9a941305b" :question/math-academy-id "q-47380" :question/problem "The function $g(s)$ describes the amount of fuel, in liters, remaining in Samuel's car after driving $s$ miles. The values of $g(s)$ for different values of $s$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $s$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(s)$ | $15$ | $13.5$ | $12.1$ | $9.4$ | $8.2$ | $6.6$ | $4.8$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change in the fuel volume when $s=8$ miles using a forward difference approximation." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(s)≈\\frac{g(s+h)-f(s)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $s=8.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{g(8+2)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(8)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.6-8.2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.6}{2} \\\\  & =-0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at $s=8$ the rate at which the fuel is changing is approximately $-0.8\\,\\text{liters/mile}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092665 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "167f04f0-c08e-51d8-acfa-2c4660083e6a" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation: Word Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb70e0ec-adee-58cc-8365-b9caa9350cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336518} {:answer/id #uuid "1d458ed0-df6b-58ec-8fe5-0ce3477b3bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.5\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336519} {:answer/id #uuid "fb74c996-e28a-5854-90b8-f16feb27f8fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336520} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba89f6c-4e74-58dc-925c-ad8541caf6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336521} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a99d56-eb10-533c-b9fa-bdc7b622da1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37.5\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb74c996-e28a-5854-90b8-f16feb27f8fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336520} :answer-field/id #uuid "06c9aa36-4fd9-5e1c-a1fa-c68d14105427" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2e860e6-e569-50bb-bb89-eb16bb320f4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-47383" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/4a7e89a828cbd660357d4834e0bcb9cb5c316dbe24419865206ba5f41872963d.png)\n\nThe power of a mobile phone emitter increases when the phone is switched on. The power output of the emitter after $t$ minutes is given by $W(t),$ where $W$ is measured in watts. The graph of $W(t)$ is shown above. \nApproximate the rate of increase in the power of the emitter when $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=2.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(1) & ≈\\frac{W(1+2)-W(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(3)-W(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{100-50}{2} \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $1$ minute, the power is increasing at a rate of approximately $25\\,\\text{watts}/\\text{minute}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6a3f2ac-404b-5dd4-8dae-e9fad7b936d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090468} {:answer/id #uuid "ff855b3b-2c71-5815-a915-22a57d790089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090469} {:answer/id #uuid "19c8d7f4-042e-5d6a-af86-786c2c8cb05a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090470} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf68d93-4152-5389-9116-6de07ca87ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090471} {:answer/id #uuid "3d9a4927-8541-5b5c-a5e1-fb42256a9452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6a3f2ac-404b-5dd4-8dae-e9fad7b936d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090468} :answer-field/id #uuid "59b488c5-ab65-5395-814b-485f6c2580ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50a7c893-eb05-5fd8-8db1-690a8664464b" :question/math-academy-id "q-47386" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/5f770f5be6b6131533dc23482281e82024737a4e5a61440dfe1baf5108786381.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=6$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" :question/worked-solution "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=6.$  Applying the above formula with $x=6$ and $h=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{g(6+4)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "419134c3-3177-5d7d-86f6-899a73338b1c" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating a Derivative From a Graph Using a Forward Difference Approximation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1409751-f544-5f4a-ab9c-c4b52f00a486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336525} {:answer/id #uuid "1306ede7-c79f-5a4b-b01c-20f48360145e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336526} {:answer/id #uuid "74a7f940-a53d-55b1-8040-b17996cdd972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336527} {:answer/id #uuid "22310289-48fc-5d49-b407-abf15eec0389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336528} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f31dd7-4596-5079-8606-deba3021c67e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1306ede7-c79f-5a4b-b01c-20f48360145e" :answer/type {:db/ident :